<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gislebert of Mons</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1150–1224</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Gilbert of Mons</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gislebert of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mons">Mons</a> was a cleric and chancellor of Count Baldwin V of Hainaut. His <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> Chronicle of Hainaut, covering the county's history to 1195, gives a detailed first-hand account of the counts' politics, marriages and diplomacy, of feudal ties in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/low-countries">Low Countries</a> and of Baldwin's dealings with the emperor and the French king. It is one of the best sources for the twelfth-century Low Countries.</p></div>
